/**
 * Lobbying (docs/lobbying.html): a fleet with a say in a town — its share of the town's carried trade
 * lately, the carriage figure the town card already draws — may ask the town for its next building,
 * standing a ghost of it on a spot that fits, or ask it to take in more ground. At each growth step that
 * would put up a building, the town rolls once: under the fleet's share it does what the fleet asked;
 * otherwise it does exactly what it would have done with nobody asking. The roll for a step is fixed
 * by the step number, so a reload never rerolls it; carrying more is the only way to move the odds.
 *
 * One preference per fleet per town. A ghost the town builds over turns red and keeps its kind; one the
 * town builds is cleared. Nothing here costs money: influence is the currency.
 *
 * Building asks were retired on 3 Nov 2026 (docs/blueprints.html): a fleet now puts up its own buildings from
 * the plans of ones it owns, and the town card asks only for more ground. The roster (LOBBY), the menu and the roll
 * stay as library code — the follies' sizes read the roster, and the lobby and culture gates drive the roll — but
 * no player surface sets a building ask, and one in an old save is let go of on load.
 */

